+   never a drop. Count: the headed pieces match the table of contents where
+   one exists. Coverage: the pieces tile the whole document with no gaps and
+   no overlaps, a body region is present, and no single body piece holds most
+   of a body over the word cap. Pointers: every line the model pointed at,
+   the title, author, source and date included, is the line it copied, or a
+   neighbour within five that is; a pointer that fails is nulled, so nothing
+   the model invented is stored. A flagged document is asked once more on
+   the same model, and once on the stronger model when it is small enough to
+   be cheap there. A text or PDF unit is one piece with the pieces under it
+   (a section with its subsections, a chapter with its scenes, a play with
+   its notes), grouped by the model, never two peers, never over the word
+   cap; a piece over the cap is split by the model inside itself until its
+   parts fit, and one that will not split is flagged. A chat unit is a run of
+   at least two turns under the cap, never across a day change when the file
